  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assessment of Water Payment Modalities for Low-Income Households in FDW Projects</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This assignment reviews billing and payment modalities used by water service providers to serve low-income households in projects supported by the Sustainable Water Fund (FDW). Through a desk study and interviews with project partners, the study documents practical approaches to improving billing, revenue collection and willingness to pay for drinking water services in rural, peri-urban and urban contexts. The analysis identifies lessons learned and provides recommendations on how innovative payment systems can strengthen the financial sustainability and scalability of water services for low-income communities.</narrative>
  </description>
